[114.868, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 2 report (Altitude)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Did:** We settled the goal, the targets, the proof and the constraints. The restatement is confirmed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The deliverable is still the original plan, unchanged, with a snapshot in `.ambition/steps/2/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Your real problem is uneven sales and not knowing what's working, so the plan needs to start by\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  measuring.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Reaching $3,000 a month needs roughly 90 orders at your current average order, or about 70 if bundles\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and gift sets lift the average to about $43.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The holiday window is already tight. It's November 13, and shipping cutoffs are close.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Your real Etsy stats aren't available, so every figure in the plan will be labelled an estimate for you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  to replace.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Changed course:** The target is no longer a generic plan. It's a week-by-week plan for a roughly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  25-listing shop, with a $150 monthly budget and 5 hours a week. It includes a scorecard, kill-or-keep rules\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and a competitor comparison.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I can't finish the whole plan in this step, so the plan file itself has not been rewritten yet. The method\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  runs the remaining work in separate steps, and the next one arrives on its own. I'll do the rewrite and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  checks there.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
