[122.113, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 3/8 · Depth\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The four statements**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **What a top practitioner would do that I didn't ask for.** An Etsy growth consultant wouldn't hand over\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a tactic menu. They'd model the funnel (visits × conversion × average order value = revenue) and find which\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  term is the bottleneck. They'd also read competitors' live listings, cut tactics that don't fit 5 hours and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  $150, and set a kill threshold on every tactic.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Rawest material.** Your Etsy Stats, which you've chosen to keep private, so I use your described\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  numbers as labelled estimates. For the market, I'd read live competitor listings, not summaries.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Methods and instruments.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - A funnel model script that recomputes every number in the plan. I'll run it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - Live competitor pages read with web search and fetch.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - A weekly schedule whose hours and spend are summed by code, not by eye.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **What shows it's right.** The script's arithmetic check, the competitor data as actually fetched, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  your weekly scorecard once you fill it with real stats.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Rewritten task:** Rebuild the plan as a funnel-driven, week-by-week sprint-then-cycle schedule for your\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  shop, with a scorecard, kill-or-keep rules and a sourced competitor table. All figures come from a checked\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  model.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll start with the competitor data and the model.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
