[389.512, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 3 report (Depth)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Did:** I rebuilt `etsy-candle-marketing-plan.md` around a funnel model (visits × conversion × order\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  value). It now has 24 dated weeks of tasks (Nov 16 to Apr 26), each capped at 5 hours. It also has a $150\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  budget table, a weekly scorecard, kill-or-keep rules, a Week 1 diagnosis, an estimates register, and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  competitor section. A snapshot is in `.ambition/steps/3/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Checked:** I wrote `.ambition/work/check_plan.py`, which reads the finished file and recomputes the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  numbers. It passes. All 24 weeks start on Mondays and sum to their stated hours (none over 5.0). All four\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  revenue scenarios, the weekly pace figures and both budget columns ($150 each) add up. This only checks the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  arithmetic. I haven't tested whether the tactics will work.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Your \"uneven sales\" may be partly chance. At about 37 orders a month, a normal month runs anywhere from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  25 to 49. So the kill-or-keep rules judge tactics on visits and clicks first, and on orders only over longer\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  windows.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Spring $3,000 is reachable mainly through a higher average order (about $40, using gift sets above\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Etsy's free-shipping threshold). Getting there on traffic alone would need more than double your visits.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - November's $2,000 is a stretch. It needs roughly double your normal pace for the rest of the month.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  December is more plausible.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Couldn't do:** Etsy blocked every page read (HTTP 403) and I didn't work around it. The competitor\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  section has only three shops' sales counts from search snippets, which may be out of date. I added a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  90-minute worksheet for you to fill in the rest in Week 7.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Changed course:** The plan now cuts the generic items (separate TikTok, wholesale, markets, press, own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  website) and parks them until after April. The first version's tactic menu, brand-positioning and risks\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sections are shorter or gone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Please check:** I assumed your 5 hours a week covers marketing only, not making or packing candles. If\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it must cover everything, the plan needs trimming.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
