[582.75, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 4 report (Challenge)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Did:** I tested the plan's assumptions against Etsy's own help pages, USPS's holiday page, fee write-ups\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and a margin model. I fixed the plan wherever a test failed, and snapshotted it to `.ambition/steps/4/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `check_plan.py` now also recomputes the margin table, and it passes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Tested and held:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The calendar dates (Black Friday Nov 27, Cyber Monday Nov 30, Valentine's Sunday Feb 14, Easter Mar 28,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Mother's Day May 9) are correct.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The Offsite Ads rates are right: 15% below $10,000 and 12% at or above it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The Etsy Ads $1 minimum is right.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Tested and wrong, now fixed:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Ad budget:** Etsy sets one shop-wide daily budget, not one per listing. The plan now uses about $2.65\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a day for November–December and about $2 a day for January–April.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Review requests:** The plan paired a discount code with the review request, which can read as an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  incentive. The code and the review ask are now on separate inserts, with no offer attached to a review.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Email:** Etsy requires opt-in consent for marketing email. The plan now says to email only people who\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  opt in and never to import buyer addresses.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Shipping cutoffs:** I replaced the placeholder with USPS's dates (Ground Advantage Dec 17, Priority\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Mail Dec 18) and set Dec 14 as the practical last order date.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Free-shipping threshold:** The $35 rule is confirmed only as a 2019 announcement. The plan now treats\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the guarantee as a decision to verify, not a default.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **New finding (the blind spot):** The plan never checked profit. Free shipping turns postage into your\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  cost. In the margin model, a $38 two-jar set earns about **$3.94** per order. A $28 jar with $7 shipping\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  paid by the buyer earns about **$13.23**. Light sets and mini add-ons are the better order-value lever, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a two-jar set needs about **$47** to reach $12 profit. The plan now has a margin table, a $12-per-order rule\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for every bundle, and a profit-per-order line in the scorecard. The margin inputs (materials $9 per jar,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  postage $8–12) are my estimates, so the conclusion holds only if your real costs are close to them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Second finding:** Most December gift revenue has to land between Black Friday and about Dec 14. That\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  makes Weeks 2–5 the weeks that decide whether December reaches $2,000.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Still unverified:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Etsy's policy pages themselves, because I only reached secondary sources.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Your real Offsite Ads status.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Your actual costs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    The plan flags each of these as something to check in Week 1.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[582.84, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 5 of pushing the work further: Range. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 5/8 · Range`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[626.147, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 5/8 · Range\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the plan is really trying to do, as verbs.** The plan's own verbs, kept as they are, are to *attract*\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  strangers who are searching, *persuade* gift buyers that the candle is worth it, *convert* visits into\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  orders, and *retain* buyers. The deeper verbs are these:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Decide:** choose where 5 hours and $150 go each week, from noisy data.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Deliver:** make and ship the right candles by hard dates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Sustain:** keep a part-timer with a day job going for 24 weeks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Protect:** keep buyers, the shop and other people from harm.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The fields, and what I'm borrowing from each:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Field | What it actually does | Direction it proposes |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Etsy growth consultant (the genre's own best practitioner) | Maps one search phrase to each listing and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  checks rank directly | Avoid your listings competing with each other, and track page-1 rank for a few target\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  phrases each week |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Operations / lean manufacturing (a field I wouldn't normally reach for) | Capacity planning, make-to-stock\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  versus make-to-order, lead times | A production calendar that sets pour dates and quantities against the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sales dates, since soy candles need time to cure |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Gift merchandising (department-store gift buyers) | Sells by recipient and price point, not by product | A\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  good/better/best ladder framed as \"for the teacher / host / mum\" |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Behaviour-change / adherence science | Fixed slots, if-then plans, a minimum version of the habit | A\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"minimum viable week\" so a bad week doesn't end the plan |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Red team: consumer-protection and product-safety review | Reads a plan for claims, disclosures, consent\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and harm | Finds who could be hurt and which rules could be broken |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  For the red team I'm using an independent agent that gets only the finished file and the goal, not my\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  reasoning. Meanwhile I'll check one fact the operations view depends on: how long soy candles take to cure.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
