[1055.911, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 6 report (Judge)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The checks:** none of them is me or another model.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - `check_plan.py` recomputes every scenario, margin figure, weekly hour total, budget and production\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  quantity from the file.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - `judge.py` tests each restatement promise and runs the same 21 feature tests on the first version and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the final. It also checks structure: tables, headings, links, placeholders and duplicated text.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - I then read the whole file cold, start to finish.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Promises:** all pass except one. The restatement promised a table of 5–10 competitor shops with price\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  points and photo counts. I couldn't deliver it. Etsy returned 403 on every page I tried, and the two roundup\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  articles I tried as a workaround were also unreachable. The plan says so plainly and gives you a 90-minute\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  worksheet to fill in during Week 7. I counted this as a disclosed gap, not a pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Against the first version:** the final is better on 14 features the first version lacked (dated\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  schedule, arithmetic, scorecard, kill-or-keep rules, margin check, policy and safety rules, and others). The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  judge caught two things I'd dropped, which I restored:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Brand positioning is back as \"Who buys, and why they'd choose you\", with a one-line angle you write in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Week 7.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Email flows are back, including a replenish reminder 6–8 weeks after signup, since a candle gets used\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  up.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cold read:** it found more than the scripts did, and I fixed all of it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The most urgent action (pour stock this weekend) was buried, so there's now a \"Start here\" box and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  section guide at the top.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - There were two contradictory price ladders; I merged them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The plan said \"hold ads until Week 3\" but never started them in Week 3.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A weekly task still compared order counts, against the Section 8 rule.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Two tasks told you to move ad budget between listings, which Etsy doesn't allow.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - There were reader-facing references to my script, a duplicated caveat, and British spellings.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A few lines overclaimed, such as \"reachable\" and \"faster than any social posting\"; they're hedged now.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Still unchecked:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - No Markdown viewer was available, so layout is verified by parsing (all 39 tables well-formed) but not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  by eye in a real viewer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The plan is now about 7,100 words against 1,600, which is a real cost. The weekly tables account for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  most of it, and the \"Start here\" box is the short path.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Whether the plan works is untested. The checks cover arithmetic, consistency and coverage.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
