[1271.015, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 7 report (Stretch)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The stretch target:** $6,000 a month in April 2027, with $3,000 reached by the end of February, two\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  months early. That is +$4,800 over today against +$1,800 for your goal, about 2.7× the growth, on the same 5\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  marketing hours and $150. Your $3,000 goal is the fallback. Sections 1–11 are unchanged apart from a header\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  line, two pointers and four new rows in the estimates register.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Did:** I added Section 12, the stretch track. Retail rises to about $3,600 (3,200 visits at 2.5% and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  $45 average order). A second channel, bulk and event orders, adds $2,400 (6 orders of about $400). A bulk\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  order of 50 mini tins earns about $184 profit, against about $13 for a retail one. Section 12 sets three\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  gates (Dec 28, Feb 15, Mar 22) for switching it on or falling back. It also has eight hours-neutral task\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  swaps, so no week goes over 5 hours. The checker recomputes every number and confirms each swap against the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  real weekly tables. It passes, and so does the judge.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Where it breaks, ranked:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    1. **Bulk demand:** the plan's 60 outreach contacts yield roughly 1–4 bulk orders, not 6. The rest would\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  have to come from Etsy search, which I can't predict.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    2. **Your time:** making, packing and marketing go from about 10.4 to about 15.3 hours a week.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    3. **Retail traffic:** you need about 1,350 more visits a month, and $60 of ads covers only 6–15% of that.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    4. **Cash:** materials come to about $1,900 a month.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    5. **Late or broken bulk orders:** these fall on fixed event dates, so Section 12 adds safety rules,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  including a written ship-by date at least 3 weeks before the event.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **My read:** $6,000 by April is unlikely. The realistic top end is about $4,000–$5,000, and only if the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  bulk channel works at all. The plan says so. Even the low case ($3,400) sits above the $3,000 fallback.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Evidence limits:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The bulk-season timing comes from vendor guides, which are directional only.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - I found no case showing this exact trajectory. One seller's $500,000 Etsy candle story exists, but I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  haven't read it, and it doesn't show this pace.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Making speeds and the outreach reply and close rates are my guesses, so they're flagged in the register.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
