[1371.364, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ## Final report\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A marketing plan for my handmade candle shop on Etsy, as a Markdown file → a dated 24-week plan (Nov 16\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  to Apr 26) for your shop.** It's built on your numbers: about $1,200 a month, 25 listings, 5 hours a week\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and $150 a month. It aims at steady monthly sales ($2,000 in each of November and December, $3,000 a month\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  by April) and gives you a way to find out what's working.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **How each part of the ask was raised:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Generic tactic menu → ranked levers.** Each one has a budget, hours and a kill-or-keep rule.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **No numbers → a funnel model.** It shows the arithmetic, and a Week 1 diagnosis tells you whether\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  listings or traffic are the bottleneck.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Revenue only → a margin check.** I found that a $38 two-jar set earns about $4 profit, against about\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  $13 for a plain jar.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **No check on feasibility → added production, safety and policy checks.** These cover a production\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  calendar with cure time, ASTM F2058 labeling, FTC gift disclosure, Etsy review and email rules, and Offsite\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Ads status.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Added a minimum viable week** (2.5 hours or less) so a bad week doesn't end the plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Better:** 14 of the 21 features I tested (dated schedule, arithmetic, scorecard, kill-or-keep rules,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  margin check, policy and safety, production calendar, shipping dates and others) were missing from the first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  version and are in the final.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Gave up:** nothing that the first version did better. My rewrite had dropped brand positioning and email\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  flows, including a replenish reminder. The judge caught both and I restored them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cost:** length. The plan is 9,201 words against 1,601. The weekly tables are most of that, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"Start here\" box is the short path. The competitor table also isn't what was promised (see below).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Check on both:** the same feature tests ran on each version. The first version passed 8 and the final\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  passed all 21 (13 of those the first version lacked), with no regressions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`check_plan.py`:** passes. All 24 weeks start on Mondays and sum to their stated hours (none over 5.0).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The funnel scenarios, weekly pace, both $150 budget columns, margin, production, stretch and gate tables\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  recompute correctly. All 49 weekday-and-date pairs are real weekdays.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`judge.py`:** passes. All 47 tables are well-formed, with no placeholders, no duplicated prose and no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  malformed links.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Known failure:** the competitor table. Etsy returned 403 on every page, and the roundup pages were also\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  unreachable. The plan has three snippet-based sales figures and a worksheet instead. I did not work around\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the block.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Independent review:** a separate agent red-teamed the plan and found 10 problems. I fixed all of them\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (the 12% Offsite Ads rate, creator-gifting disclosure, safety, ad budget, timing and others).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Not checked:** no Markdown viewer was available, so layout was verified by parsing, not by eye. Whether\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the plan works is untested. The checks cover arithmetic, consistency and coverage.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Target:** $6,000 a month in April 2027, with $3,000 reached by the end of February.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **How far it got:** the route is built (Section 12). It adds bulk and event orders (6 a month at about\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  $400) to retail of about $3,600, with three gates and eight hours-neutral swaps. The $3,000 fallback is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  intact.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **My read:** $6,000 is unlikely. The realistic top end is about $4,000–$5,000, and the low case lands at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  $3,400.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Where it breaks:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    1. **Bulk demand:** 60 outreach contacts yield roughly 1–4 orders, not 6.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    2. **Your time:** about 15.3 hours a week instead of 10.4.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    3. **Retail traffic:** $60 of ads covers only 6–15% of the extra visits needed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    4. **Cash:** about $1,900 a month in materials.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    5. **Late bulk orders:** these fall on fixed event dates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Files:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - `plan-tools/check_plan.py`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - `plan-tools/judge.py`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - `plan-tools/run_checks.sh`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - `CLAUDE.md` (a short note on how to run it and what proved it)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - `.claude/commands/check-plan.md` (the `/check-plan` command)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rerun:** `sh plan-tools/run_checks.sh`, or `/check-plan`, after any change to a number. The one expected\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  FAIL line is the competitor table.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Snapshots:** `.ambition/first/` holds the first version (never edited). `.ambition/steps/2` to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/steps/8` hold each step's copy.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions made**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - You never told me to use my judgement, so every answer in the restatement was yours. The plan's own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  assumptions are listed in Section 11 for you to replace. The main ones are the 1,850 visits, the 2%\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  conversion, the $9 per jar and $8–12 postage costs, and that your 5 hours cover marketing only (Decision 5).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions (the most urgent left; all five are in Section 13)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Does your 5 hours include making and packing? (by Mon Nov 16).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *For (a), marketing only:* keeps every task.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *For (b), everything:* matches a day-job schedule, but cuts about half the tasks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Pick:* whichever is true. If it's \"everything\", ask me for the cut-down plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Etsy's free-shipping guarantee (by Tue Nov 24).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *For turning it on now:* may help search placement, but you pay postage and the current effect is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  unconfirmed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *For leaving it off:* keeps about $13 profit per plain jar.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Pick:* off until at least two bundles earn $12 or more profit with free shipping.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **When to start Etsy Ads (Mon Nov 16).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Week 1:* gets data earliest, but spends on listings that may convert poorly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Week 3:* lets you fix the top listings first, but loses two weeks of the holiday window.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Pick:* follow the Week 1 diagnosis (Week 1 if conversion is 1.5% or higher, otherwise Week 3).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **Insurance (quote by Fri Nov 20, buy by Mon Jan 4).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *For buying before the holidays:* full cover, at a cost I couldn't verify.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *For buying before gifting or bulk:* covers the new risks before they start.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Against waiting:* you'd be uninsured while volume rises.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Pick:* get a quote now and buy before gifted sets or bulk orders.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  5. **Run the stretch overlay (Mon Dec 28).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *For:* about $184 profit per bulk order.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Against:* about 5 more hours a week of making, and risk of late event orders.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Pick:* only if December is at least $1,800 and you can add that time.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Metrics since 2026-11-13T08:05:03Z (cost: /cost, or total_cost_usd in headless JSON)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  total   in 150 · out 172.4k (think 91.8k) · cache read 8.09M · write 279.1k · hit 97% · 67 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  model   sonnet-5-5: in 150 · out 172.4k (think 91.8k) · cache read 8.09M · write 279.1k · hit 97% · 67 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  agent   main: in 144 · out 153.6k (think 78.3k) · cache read 8.06M · write 227.6k · hit 97% · 64 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  agent   general-purpose ×1: in 6 · out 18.8k (think 13.5k) · cache read 36.4k · write 51.5k · hit 41% · 3\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n"]
